<section id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Normalized FF-KV.</h4>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The feature vectors of SAE are typically normalized, whereas those in FF are not.
If a particular feature vector <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{W}_{V[i,:]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑾</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{W}_{V[i,:]}</annotation></semantics></math> has a large norm, the magnitude of its corresponding activation may be underestimated.
To handle this potential concern, we normalize each row of <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{W}_{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{W}_{V}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the discounted vector norm is weighted to activations.
We refer to the method with this post-correction as <span id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Normalized (TopK) FF-KV</span>:</p>
<table id="S3.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
